From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] launcher: keep the baked app after an early exit

Applies to the launcher Steam installs (app 3029110).

An app that exits within 30 seconds of launch had its baked Android data
cleared, which drops its folder grants along with the install. Quitting
quickly is common on a handheld, and apps such as emulators then lose
access to the folder they were given. The logcat dump stays.

---
--- a/lepton
+++ b/lepton
@@ -210,11 +210,6 @@
             if [[ -n "${LEPTON_DUMP_LOGCAT:-}" ]] || [[ "${EARLY_SHUTDOWN}" == "1" ]]; then
                 println "Dumping logcat to $(logcat_debug_dir)"
                 dump_logcat "$(logcat_debug_dir)"
-
-                if [[ "${EARLY_SHUTDOWN}" == "1" ]]; then
-                    # Clearing baked app data in this case since something might be wrong.
-                    clear_baked_app_data "early exit"
-                fi
             fi
 
             kill_container "${LEPTON_CONTEXT}" --quiet
